ok - an unknown reading never counts as clean: a closed or clearing gate holds until a real reading clears it, including a gate that is otherwise omitted, and an open gate stays unjudged
ok - closed gates outlive the budget's freshness window, so only a clean reading reopens admission
ok - a native Windows home reads memory, cores, load, and power from the PowerShell host view, and falls back to the ceiling without it
ok - admission counts lanes started since the last publish against the damped budget, so a burst cannot exceed it
ok - --admit and --spawn-gate skip process attribution and the GPU probe their verdict does not read
ok - --spawn-gate applies the verdict only when config/lane-capacity declares admit-spawns, and refuses when the file cannot be read
